<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umhlanga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Umhlanga reed dance, Reed Dance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umhlanga, the reed dance, is an annual ceremony of the Swazi Kingdom (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>), held in late August or early September. Tens of thousands of unmarried girls and young women cut tall reeds and bring them to the queen mother's royal village at Ludzidzini to repair its windbreak, then dance before the king and queen mother. It is among the largest cultural events in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umhlanga.jpg" alt="Umhlanga" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amada44 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reed_Dance_Festival_2006-001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
